The two components
Component	Marks	How it is scored
Lane identification	20	Fraction of frames where lane matches the ground truth
Lane centre	30	How close center_x is to the true lane centre

Lane centre tolerance. A lane is roughly 315 px wide in the frame, so your center_x does not have to be exact:
Error against the ground truth	Credit
within 30 px	full
within 60 px	half
beyond 60 px	none
the lane for that frame was wrong	none

That last row matters: the centre of the wrong lane is not the centre of your lane, however close the number looks. Get the lane right first.

Frames you give up on still count. Returning "unknown" / -1 on a frame where the lane was clearly visible scores zero on both components, the same as a wrong answer. Reporting failure honestly costs you nothing extra and makes your own debugging far easier

