2. Run the evaluation

Run it from task1c/, the folder holding your completed lane_detection.py with the clips beside it in public/:

task1c/
├── lane_detection.py
└── public/
    ├── clip_01.mp4
    └── …

The skipped column is the ambiguous frames - mid lane-change, or the divider out of view - which are excluded for everyone and cost you nothing.
Terminal window

eyantra-autoeval evaluate --year 2026 --theme NV --task 1c

The tool finds your lane_detection.py and the dataset, checks every clip is 640 x 480, then calls your detect_lane() on every frame and compares the output against the ground truth. It prints a per-clip breakdown and your public-set score:

